# Line endings are pinned to LF for every text file, in the repository *and* in
# the working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: this repo has no .gitattributes, so line endings were
# left to each contributor's `core.autocrlf`. On Windows that defaults to true,
# which checks every file out as CRLF — while .prettierrc sets
# `endOfLine: "lf"`. The result was `npm run format:check` failing on all 255
# tracked source files, including ones nobody had ever edited, which made the
# check useless for spotting genuine style problems. The committed content was
# already LF; only the Windows working copy differed.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf per-repository, so everyone gets identical
# line endings regardless of platform or personal git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted — doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
